    "created_at": "2026-11-24T22:51:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T22:51:19Z",
    "body": "PR #3912 (for #3891) is merged. It covers this issue. Under control or wear compensation, `contour_comp::door` refuses a Linear lead-in or lead-out, on both the wall side and the bore side. The refusal text names the descent at the lead-in's start before G41/G42 engages, as this issue does. The only case left is Computer compensation. There is no register there, so nothing can cut the wall. I close this issue as a duplicate of #3891.\n",
